    {
      "value": "<p>Some eleven thousand shallow rectangular cuts in the salt crust, arranged in blocks with walls of packed crust between them, each block worked and then left for a term of years. Brine is let in, taken out and let in again on a schedule that survived the suspension of contact and presumably still does. The last direct observation was in 2297.</p>",
